<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!-- Apple has required this manifest since 2024. An upload without it is
         rejected, and one that overstates what it collects is a promise the
         product then has to keep.

         Every array below is empty, and each is empty for a reason worth
         stating rather than left to be assumed. This is the same claim
         `prv-security` makes in code and architecture rule 10 enforces in the
         sandbox; here it is made in the form Apple reads. -->

    <!-- Nothing is tracked. No advertising identifier is read, no profile is
         built for anybody else's purposes, and nothing is joined with data from
         another company. -->
    <key>NSPrivacyTracking</key>
    <false/>

    <key>NSPrivacyTrackingDomains</key>
    <array/>

    <!-- Nothing is collected. The application's whole design is that the user's
         music and projects stay on their machine: the core performs no
         input or output at all (ADR-0001), and the macOS sandbox has no
         network-client entitlement, so an outbound connection is impossible
         rather than merely unused.

         Cloud synchronisation, when it ships, adds entries here in the same
         commit as the consent screen and the entitlement it depends on. -->
    <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes</key>
    <array/>

    <!-- No required-reason API is used.

         Checked rather than assumed: the four categories Apple asks about are
         file timestamps, system boot time, disk space and user defaults. The
         application reads directories and creates them — `createDirectory`,
         `fileExists`, `contentsOfDirectory` — none of which are on the list,
         and it stores no preferences in `UserDefaults`. Timestamps that reach
         the project log are supplied by the caller, not read from the
         filesystem, because ADR-0001 keeps the core away from the clock.

         An entry added here later should be added because a call was added,
         and the two belong in the same commit. -->
    <key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes</key>
    <array/>
</dict>
</plist>
